{number: 50}
{title: Have Thine Own Way, Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own way!
Thou art the Potter,
I am the clay.
Mould me and make me
After Thy will,
While I am waiting,
Yielded and still.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own way!
Search me and try me,
Master, today!
Whiter than snow, Lord,
Wash me just now,
As in Thy presence
Humbly I bow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own way!
Wounded and weary,
Help me, I pray.
Power, all power
Surely is Thine!
Touch me and heal me,
Savior divine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own way!
Hold o'er my being
Absolute sway!
Fill with Thy Spirit
Till all shall see
Christ only, always,
Living in me!
{end_of_verse}
